    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch02-09: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.65";
    dc:description "The predicted exponent and outcome are unambiguous, and published public trait records permit a restricted comparative test. Coverage from fleas to horses with matched geometry is inadequate, requiring substantial compilation for the full scope.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Compile maximal jump height, body length and limb geometry for similarly constructed animals, then test whether absolute height has a size exponent of zero after controlling lever ratios. A consistent nonzero scaling exponent would refute the stated law.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Finding animals that satisfy similar construction across a wide size range is difficult.", "Jump-height measurements are sparse and methodologically heterogeneous.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.8"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch02-09--gpt--dataset-1>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.645"^^xsd:double;
